{"name":"Hot Potato","hex":"#e39e66","fetched":"2026-10-23","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hot potato","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A child's game in which players pass a ball or other item between them, with the object of avoiding being left holding the item when time expires.","An unwanted problem that is awkward or delicate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot_potato"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hot potato","blocks":[{"text":"Hot potato is a party game that involves players gathering in a circle and tossing a small object such as a beanbag or even a soft ball to each other while music plays. The player who is holding the object when the music stops is eliminated."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_potato","wikidata":"Q5910245"},{"title":"Hot Potato (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Hot Potato is a puzzle video game developed by Pukka Games and published by BAM! Entertainment for the Game Boy Advance. It was released in North America on June 28, 2001, and in the United Kingdom on November 2, 2001."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/29/Hot_Potato_Coverart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Potato_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q5910242"},{"title":"Potato","blocks":[{"text":"The potato is a starchy tuberous vegetable native to the Americas that is consumed as a staple food in many parts of the world. Potatoes are underground stem tubers of the plant Solanum tuberosum, a perennial in the nightshade family Solanaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Patates.jpg/330px-Patates.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potato","wikidata":"Q10998"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/29/Hot_Potato_Coverart.jpg/250px-Hot_Potato_Coverart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_